      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T02:56:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Get it 😊\n1. Our android OS has many important cfs tasks, such as RenderThread, PMS..., we call them \"user-aware threads\" and give them different \"user-aware property\"(which is not the same concept with nice value used in scheduler). With this \"user-aware property\", we have an ability to control kernel resources more granularly.\n2. We want this \"user-aware property\" to be inherited across rtmutex, also, we will use rtmutex in our feature.\n3. \"user-aware property\" will be mapped to different rtmutex_waiter prios (100, 101, 102...). And the DEFAULT_PRIO is just used for those normal cfs tasks we don\u0027t care about.\n4. The rtmutex owner will inherit \"user-aware property\"(this member is saved in struct task_struct) once the \"user-aware thread\" is blocked on it, and clear it\u0027s \"user-aware property\" when unlock.",
